    [BugFix][EPLB] Support flattened DeepSeek V4.1 text config (#20240)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    Applies the same EPLB text-configuration fix as
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm-ascend/pull/19514 to `main`.
    
    Fixes #18166.
    
    DeepSeek V4.1 with Dynamic EPLB fails during EPLB warmup with:
    
    ```text
    AttributeError: 'DeepseekV41Config' object has no attribute 'text_config'
    ```
    
    `VllmEplbAdaptor` currently assumes any model exposing `language_model`
    has `model.config.text_config`. vLLM's `DeepseekV41Config` flattens the
    released text configuration onto the top-level config.
    
    This change uses `model.config.get_text_config()`, which returns the
    nested text config for multimodal models such as Qwen/GLM and returns
    the top-level config for flattened DeepSeek V4.1 configurations.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No public API or configuration change.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - Rebased onto current `main` and verified `git diff --check`.
    - Built and ran the main matching Ascend environment with V1 Model
    Runner.
    - Existing EPLB adaptor unit tests passed: `pytest -q
    tests/ut/eplb/adaptor`.
    - Real-weight Qwen multimodal MoE validation passed with TP2, Expert
    Parallel, and Dynamic EPLB.
    - GLM `Glm4vMoeForConditionalGeneration` validation passed with TP2,
    Expert Parallel, Dynamic EPLB, image request, and text request.
    - vLLM main:
    https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/commit/544f182d9f0c9bfe8bd7645525951d5e3692a542
    
    Signed-off-by: x00946744 <xingbowen1@huawei.com>
    Co-authored-by: x00946744 <xingbowen1@huawei.com>

